    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0452" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg356"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic">December 11,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 352.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    dispatch from the United States minister at Teheran, Persia, inclosing a
                    petition from American citizens resident in Tabriz and Urumia, requesting some
                    acknowledgment from the State Department of the services of Her Majesty’s
                    consul-general, Mr. Cecil J. Wood, in their behalf.</p>
                <p>You are accordingly instructed to express to the foreign office, in suitable
                    terms, the thanks of the Government for Mr. Wood’s timely services.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




